          "id": "F1",
          "text": "Preserve official return checks when the checkout cannot fit on disk\n\nConsumer: packet tooling owner; proposed support helper only.\n\nThe supplied archive was about 64 MB, while the ordinary filesystem had no\nfree space. A complete repository materialization also exceeded the available\ntemporary filesystem. The official builder correctly rejects absent original\nshared source, so a partial working extraction cannot be packaged directly.\n\n`checks/tooling/memory_package/package_in_memory.py` provides a concrete\ncandidate adapter: verify the original archive and member hashes, reconstruct\nthe entire original WORK in a process-local memory filesystem, overlay actual\nreview bytes, require every initially materialized original path to remain\npresent, and invoke the original builder without changing its validation.\nValidate the emitted archive again outside the adapter. Its tests must compare\nnormal and memory-built bytes and retain rejection of modified manifests,\nbaselines, shared files, and unauthorized added source. The helper is a local\nproposal; no shared implementation or approval is changed by this return.\n\nUse the official fresh `replay-return --runtime-closure` after packaging when\nstorage permits. This checks a fresh declared dependency extraction, real Git\npatch applicability and exact changed-byte equality; it does not run tests or\nextract the entire source packet. Exact receipts define the verified scope.\n\nBounded owner adoption test: compare byte-identical returns for the same small\nvalid workspace, require all tamper tests to reject, then replay one real\npacket delta with the public command. Reject on any output divergence,\nweakened source check, silent deletion recovery, or dependency leakage. Keep\nthe original on-disk builder as the reference path. The optional adapter needs\npinned pyfakefs 6.2.0 and process memory; the shear prototype does not."
        }
